    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** (67.88) and **Lawrence Butler** (64.46) stand out as our most robust plays, both benefiting from favorable matchups against mid-rotation arms. **Jonathan Aranda** is locked into the #2 hole against Alcantara, where his 0.386 xwOBA makes him an essential start, while **Lawrence Butler** leverages a +13% dynamic platoon edge against Burrows. Although **Luis Arraez** (60.99) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (59.04) are subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status, their projection against Taillon remains strong; their floor is slightly muted by an \"In\" wind factor, but their contact-heavy profiles against a hittable right-hander keep them firmly in the starting rotation.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Geraldo Perdomo** (48.89), who was the first cut from the active lineup. While he offers some utility, his projection against Cavalli was insufficient to displace the power-upside provided by **Matt Chapman** (58.86) or the speed-adjusted profile of **Jung Hoo Lee**. Elsewhere, we must navigate a high-risk encounter for **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (52.83) as he faces the elite arm of deGrom. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an automatic starter in most contexts, the SP skill penalty and potential for deGrom to suppress stolen base opportunities necessitate a slight regression in his daily expectation. We remain cautious regarding the weather and confirmed lineups for the Taillon start, but as it stands, our focus remains on protecting our game caps while maximizing the platoon advantages for **Jonathan Aranda** and **Lawrence Butler**.",
